# Portfolio Images Setup

## Required Images for Portfolio

To complete your portfolio setup, you need to copy the following images from your VS Code project to the appropriate directories:

### Profile and Hero Images:
- `Adiba_pic.jpg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/` (update path in PersonalInfo table)

### Experience Images:
- `hult1.jpg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`
- `SheStem.jpg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`
- `casecrackfinalist.jpg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`
- `KBEC_member.jpg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`

### Project Images:
- `portfilo.png` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`
- `pawpal.jpeg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`
- `fitnesstracker.jpeg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`
- `casecrack.jpg` → Copy to root directory or `~/Uploads/`

### Resume:
- `Adiba_CV.pdf` → Copy to root directory

## Database Setup

Run the SQL script `Database/portfolio-schema.sql` to create all necessary tables and insert sample data.

## File Structure After Setup:
```
adminpanel/
├── Home.aspx (Public Portfolio)
├── Default.aspx (Admin Dashboard)
├── Login.aspx (Admin Login)
├── Projects.aspx (Project Management)
├── Content/
│   └── portfolio-style.css (Your original styles)
├── Scripts/
│   └── portfolio.js (Your original functionality)
├── Uploads/ (Project images uploaded via admin)
├── Adiba_pic.jpg (Profile image)
├── hult1.jpg, SheStem.jpg, etc. (Experience images)
├── portfilo.png, pawpal.jpeg, etc. (Project images)
└── Adiba_CV.pdf (Resume)
```

Your portfolio is now ready with all the original VS Code functionality!